  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>99</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The number of elements in domain and codomain is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99</mn></math>.</p><p>Now, let us assume&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/313916fe-0c5f-412d-a252-42d6dc5764fb-acf71c03-cfeb-496b-a99b-532940d809da-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 300px;\" /></p><p>Now as per diagram we have only&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;way for arranging&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>99</mn></mfenced></math>,</p><p>Similarly if we choose&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>98</mn></math>&nbsp;then again we have only&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;way for arranging&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>99</mn></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So we can see the arrangement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>99</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;depends upon&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So number of ways for choosing&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts></math></p></blockquote>",
